    {
        id bug
        title "Correctness bugs surfaced by the panic/unrepresentable audit"
        kind @fix
        children (
            {
                id bug.relation-pairing
                title "ColumnPairs: relation join zip-truncation silently returns wrong rows on arity mismatch"
                deps (decide.schema-comments)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T12:33:24.161274Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit: src/query/helper.rs:893-894 zips from_col/to_col Identity iterators; zip truncates to the shorter side, emitting an under-constrained join — wrong rows, silently. Same def in DDL (relation.rs:422-433) iterates independently and PG rejects with 42804. Remedy is the structural fix: replace the two Identity fields with a ColumnPairs newtype (non-empty Vec of (DynIden, DynIden) pairs) so unbalanced arity cannot exist. Readers to update: loader.rs, schema/entity.rs, link.rs; DeriveRelation output changes shape but not behavior. Bumps entity.relation.def and query.build.join. Also worthwhile while in the struct: is_owner+rel_type collapse into one closed enum (contradiction currently renders a correct join with a backwards FK). Deps on decide.schema-comments only for the schema/entity.rs footprint."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T19:11:36.703806Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T19:11:55.989469Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "The audit's suggested is_owner+rel_type collapse is REJECTED on the implementing agent's analysis, accepted by the lead: all four combinations are reachable and meaningful (rel_type is cardinality, is_owner is FK direction; rev() legitimately yields HasMany with is_owner=false by negating one axis). Collapsing would rename a genuine product type without closing an illegal state. The deferred consequence in [dec:pgorm:invalid-states-unrepresentable] does not apply here."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id bug.empty-not-in
                title "Empty NOT IN renders always-false; correct semantics are always-true"
                deps (pgparse.oracle)
