            {
                id bug.char-render
                title "Value::Char rendering panics on U+0080..FF and mis-renders higher chars via byte narrowing"
                deps (bug.empty-not-in)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T12:33:39.009301Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit: query_builder.rs:1168 renders Value::Char via from_utf8(&[*v as u8]).unwrap() — panics for any char whose low byte is >= 0x80 ('é' U+00E9), and silently renders the WRONG character for chars above U+00FF with a low byte < 0x80 ('—' U+2014 -> 0x14). Reachable via Display for Value, sea_value_to_json_value, inject_parameters, and inline constant rendering. Also value.rs:1226 does the same from_utf8 unwrap in to-json. Fix: render the char directly. The spec is WRONG about this (sql.render.value-literals claims lossy-but-successful narrowing) — bump and correct it; sql.value.to-json may bump too."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T16:53:09.178481Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id bug.window-position
                title "WINDOW clause renders after ORDER BY/LIMIT/locking; PG requires it before ORDER BY"
                deps (bug.char-render)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T12:33:46.917044Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit: prepare_select_statement writes ORDER BY (query_builder.rs:262), LIMIT/OFFSET (:273), locking (:275), THEN the named WINDOW clause (:280). PostgreSQL grammar places WINDOW between HAVING and ORDER BY, so window() combined with any of those renders a syntax error; existing tests only exercise window in isolation. Plain rendering-order fix; bumps sql.render.window (and check sql.render.select-order's clause-order claim). Add a combined window+order_by+limit test."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T16:08:57.617509Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Oracle expansion of scope: the position fix alone is not enough. (1) Named windows render without parentheses — WINDOW \"w\" AS PARTITION BY ... is invalid even in isolation; PG requires WINDOW \"w\" AS (PARTITION BY ...). (2) The six window_* tests all render unparseable SQL for a second reason: OVER is being attached to a bare column expression in projection contexts where PG rejects it — read oracle_pins_window_clause_parens and the assert_eq_unparsed! sites in window.rs (12 marked) for the full picture. Fix all three defects together and flip the pins + the 12 unparsed markers to oracle-checked assertions. sql.render.window and possibly sql.ast.window-statement bump."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T17:26:32.961595Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
