            {
                id connect-tls
                title "Expose TLS-capable construction through the standard DatabasePool API"
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-05T14:54:40.040357Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit CONFIRMED, harder than the known gap: there is NO route to a DatabasePool with TLS at all, and the spec's stated workaround is wrong. All three entry points hard-code NoTls (database/mod.rs:37,62,91). pgorm-pool is fully TLS-generic and Pool is TLS-erased (Box<dyn Connect>, lib.rs:94,116-124), so a TLS pgorm_pool::Pool is buildable — but DatabasePool's field is pub(crate) with no constructor/From, and ConnectionTrait is never implemented for pgorm_pool::Object, so the spec's \"assemble a Manager directly\" (conn.md:26-28) yields a pool no ORM machinery runs on. Scenario: any managed PG requiring TLS (RDS force_ssl, Cloud SQL, Azure, Neon, Supabase) — connect fails at handshake and nothing reachable through pgorm fixes it. SEVERITY HIGH: adoption blocker for cloud PostgreSQL. Fix: connect_with_tls<T: MakeTlsConnect<Socket>+...>(config, tls) (+builder variant) or one-line From<pgorm_pool::Pool> for DatabasePool; Pool being TLS-erased makes this additive. Effort S. Bumps conn.pool+2→+3 (rule both mandates NoTls and asserts the false workaround). Shares root cause with connect-manager-options — sealed DatabasePool + manager frozen before any caller hook; consider one combined entry point."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-05T19:51:09.445413Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
