                        kind @note
                        text "Audit CONFIRMED as a defect, spec-documented as inherited quirk, ZERO in-tree callers but public API via re-export chain (pgorm::pgorm_query::sea_value_to_json_value). Four rots in value.rs:1329-1395: (1) panics on non-UTF-8 Bytes (:1365 from_utf8 unwrap — pgorm-query does NOT deny unwrap_used, no allow needed); (2) chrono None arms missing → ChronoDate(None) becomes JSON string \"NULL\" not Json::Null, Some keeps SQL quotes (\"'2020-01-01'\"); (3) Decimal → to_f64 lossy (28 digits → ~16); (4) Float/Double NaN/inf → serde_json Null, indistinguishable from SQL NULL. u64 arm is exact — no defect there. Spec sem:sql.value.to-json specifies the panic and \"NULL\"-string verbatim (\"current behaviour, inherited and unchanged\"). Fix: make total and typed — Bytes → hex string, Decimal → string, explicit Chrono None → Null + unquoted ISO Some, explicit NaN policy. Effort M; breaking only for consumers of the current shape (none in-tree). Rewrites sem:sql.value.to-json (+1) + /test facet. Candidate for DELETION instead — zero callers; deleting the function entirely is the fork-consistent alternative (like Inserter/Deleter/expr_as_). Decide delete-vs-fix at implementation."
